<title>ESTONIA: ONE WEEK, ONE MONTH INTERBANK RATES EASE.</title>
<headline>ONE WEEK, ONE MONTH INTERBANK RATES EASE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average interbank loan rates</p>
<p>eased slightly for one week and one month, but were stable for</p>
<p>three months, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;One reason for the decline was Tallinna Pank and Hoiupank</p>
<p>took some new issues and are waitng to invest,&quot; said Ege</p>
<p>Metsandi from Hansapank's interest rate products office.</p>
<p>Metsandi added that the rates could fall further in the</p>
<p>coming week as Uhispank's new medium term note for 30 million</p>
<p>German marks comes on line.</p>
<p> TALIBOR/TALIBID    1Week     1Month     3Months</p>
<p> June  4	    5.08/4.08  5.90/4.90  7.35/6.35</p>
<p> May  28	    5.20/4.20  5.93/4.93  7.35/6.35</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9202/1 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
